.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIlibmpq\fP reads and creates MPQ v1 and v2 archives, including embedded
MPQ containers. MPQ v3/v4 and HET/BET tables are not supported.
.SS "Archive Opening and Custom I/O"
Open filesystem archives with \fBlibmpq__archive_open\fP(3) or provide a
borrowed random-access callback through \fBlibmpq__archive_open_io\fP(3).
A negative archive offset enables embedded-header scanning. Clones own
independent read state; close each archive handle when finished.
.SS "Logical Member Streams"
Use \fBlibmpq__stream_open\fP(3) or
\fBlibmpq__stream_open_name\fP(3) for incremental decoded reads and
seeking. Streams own a private archive clone and are consumed by
\fBlibmpq__stream_close\fP(3). Complete reads use
\fBlibmpq__file_read\fP(3).
Patch-file members instead expose their decoded, unapplied PTCH bodies through
\fBlibmpq__patch_payload_size\fP(3) and
\fBlibmpq__patch_payload_read\fP(3).
.SS "Archive Creation and Writers"
Create MPQ v1/v2 archives with \fBlibmpq__archive_create\fP(3).
Add complete buffers or paths with the archive-add calls, or use the
writer begin/write/finish lifecycle for streamed members. Writer finish
consumes the member writer; archive close finalizes and consumes the
archive handle. Encrypted random-access writing is not supported.
.SS "Transactional Updates"
\fBlibmpq__update_begin\fP(3) stages modifications to ordinary or
embedded MPQs in a distinct handle. Authenticated MPQE updates use
\fBlibmpq__update_begin_mpqe\fP(3). Replace, remove, and rename affect
only the working copy until commit atomically publishes it; abort
discards it. Both commit and abort consume the update handle.
.SS "Patch Archives"
The patch creation API stages replacement and deletion entries without
changing the base archive. Finish publishes a new patch artifact; abort
discards it, and both consume the patch handle. Ordinary and
MPQE-wrapped patch artifacts have separate begin calls. No public
patch-view composition API is provided.
.SS Signatures
\fBlibmpq__archive_signatures\fP(3) detects stored signatures;
\fBlibmpq__archive_verify\fP(3) verifies one type using a caller-supplied
public key. Writer signing is configured with
\fBlibmpq__archive_sign\fP(3) or \fBlibmpq__patch_sign\fP(3) and
performed at finalization. No default or product-specific keys are
built in.
.SS MPQE
MPQE operations require explicit caller-supplied authentication material.
Internal weak signatures work in MPQE-wrapped MPQs, but no external
strong-signature transport is defined. Creation and transactional updates
use private plaintext staging files; cleanup after abnormal termination
is best effort.
.SS "Metadata and Integrity"
Archive, file, and block queries expose sizes, flags, and version-100
\fB(attributes)\fP rows. Complete lossless file reads automatically
check available CRC32/MD5 and usable sector Adler-32 data.
\fBlibmpq__file_verify\fP(3) performs selected explicit comparisons;
lossy ADPCM may legitimately differ from source-byte checksums.
